WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
Success needs evidence beyond hours saved.

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:05.920
We propose three primary
measures for the banking pilot.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:10.160
First, detect every approved
critical payment fault that we

00:00:10.203 --> 00:00:14.080
deliberately introduce.
Second, exercise every critical

00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:17.840
scenario with reviewed
assertions and a valid result.

00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:22.320
Third, make each release decision
traceable to its requirements,

00:00:22.387 --> 00:00:24.880
build, test data and raw results.

00:00:25.104 --> 00:00:29.680
Then check the foundation: can the team
repeat runs reliably, validate agreed

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:34.000
behaviors against the real provider,
and help a second squad run independently?

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.760
These measures have no recorded
baseline or after result yet.

00:00:37.973 --> 00:00:41.840
We will compare today's workflow,
modernized quality engineering,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.600
and AI assistance on that
foundation. Fewer escaped defects

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.760
and emergency fixes are business
aims to validate across releases.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.360
A complete evidence pack can still
recommend stopping a release.
